Thanks for all the replies.

Here's how it works for me in Nethack 1.4f: You transcribe a spellbook
and you know the spell permanently, and the spellbook disappears. You
can only lose spells if you read a scroll of amnesia. This was nice
because you didn't have to carry a library around the dungeon with
you. The only downside was that if you failed to learn the spell, you
also lost the book. It seems that in newer versions you still keep the
book if you fail to learn it.

In Nethack 2.2 and 2.3, you lose the spellbook when you transcribe it,
and you also lose the spell after you cast it X times (seems like
around 10?) so that really sucks. Spellbooks are rare so really your
odds of re-learning the spell are slim. Basically, they become like
wands, with limited charges, but at least you don't have to carry
them.

Maybe I'll try the newer versions, but the game has become almost too
complicated for me, or it's just the nostalgia of playing the same
game I played 20 years ago.



